{
  "abstract": "Two existence theorems on unit fractions, each checked by the Lean kernel from an explicit or implicit witness. (1) The coprime variant of Erdős Problem #307 with 1 excluded: finite sets P, Q of integers greater than 1, each pairwise coprime, with (Σ_{p∈P} 1/p)(Σ_{q∈Q} 1/q) = 1. The statement is formal-conjectures' erdos_307.variants.coprime_one_notMem, listed there and on erdosproblems.com as having no known examples. The witness has 973 elements, most too large to write down. It is encoded by 914 small \"deviations\" and certified by a residue checker whose soundness is proved in Lean. (2) An all-odd solution of Znám's problem: 24 odd integers greater than 1, each a proper divisor of the product of the others plus 1. No all-odd solution was known (Brenton and Joo, 1995).",
